I fixed #1170 and committed it as c9b8245e. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is now read only when the provider is anthropic, so it no longer goes out as a bearer token to ollama, custom proxies, OpenAI, Bedrock and the rest.

What changed. The generic API_KEY and a config-file api_key still work as fallbacks for every provider. The install docs call API_KEY the "generic fallback", so it stays. The plan named one place to fix, and I found the same problem in four:
• The main key lookup (src/cli.rs), which the plan named.
• `yoyo review` has its own key lookup in src/dispatch_sub.rs with the same fallback. It also refused to run on ollama/custom with no key, which the main path allows, so I fixed that in the same diff. Otherwise review on ollama would have gone from working (by leaking the key) to refusing.
• The setup wizard check (src/setup.rs) counted ANTHROPIC_API_KEY as "a key is set" for any provider. That would skip the wizard and start the REPL with no key. I added a way to test it without touching the real environment, plus a unit test.
• Error advice. Four hints told custom/ollama users to export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, which those providers no longer read. They now name API_KEY.

Test. The new tests/provider_key_canary.rs runs the built binary with a cleared environment against a local stub server that records the auth headers:
• custom and ollama: the request still goes out, the fake key appears nowhere, and the bearer is the not-needed placeholder.
• anthropic: the fake key does arrive as x-api-key. This proves the other rows aren't passing just because nothing was sent.
• `API_KEY`: still used as the fallback for custom.
• openai with only the Anthropic key: stops before sending anything, exits 1, and names OPENAI_API_KEY.
• `yoyo review`: reaches ollama and custom without the fake key.

Against the old code the custom/ollama/API_KEY/openai rows failed; custom received Bearer sk-ant-CANARY1170. I also put each piece of old code back one at a time and the matching new assertion failed by name, then restored it.

Before and after (-p hi, only ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set):
• Before: Bedrock got a 403 and OpenAI a 401, each with a hint saying the Anthropic key "was sent instead". Those runs sent my fake key to the real AWS and OpenAI endpoints.
• After: both stop with No API key found. Set AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID … or Set OPENAI_API_KEY … and send nothing.

One other behaviour change: if ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set but empty and API_KEY is set, anthropic now uses API_KEY. Before, the empty variable blocked it.

Docs: updated CLAUDE.md's provider-key bullet (keeping the old claim marked as superseded), installation.md, common-issues.md (whose quoted error text was also out of date), ARCHITECTURE.md, and a Security entry in CHANGELOG. I also updated the copy of the lookup order in providers_key_tests.rs.

Evolve loop: not affected. .yoyo.toml has provider = "anthropic" and every workflow exports ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.

fmt, clippy, build, the full cargo test run and harness_logic.sh (336/336) all pass. I tested every case the plan asked about, so the commit says "Fixes #1170".
